logical backup: 

	- exporting your table to a flat file.
	- can be taken at table level, group of tables, schema, database and group of databases
	- cannot apply PITR on top of restored logical backup
	- pg_dump, psql or pg_restore
	
export
======
/usr/pgsql-18/bin/pg_dump -U kfc_user -d kfc_db -t emp > emp.sql

import
======
/usr/pgsql-18/bin/psql -U kfc_user -d kfc_db < emp.sql


pg_dump -U kfc_user -d kfc_db -t emp -Fc -f emp.bkp			#custom format, cannot read, compression is possible
pg_dump -U kfc_user -d kfc_db -t emp -Fp -f emp.plain		#can read
pg_dump -U kfc_user -d kfc_db -t emp -Ft -f emp.tar			#tar format, we hardly use it, o/s tar
pg_dump -U kfc_user -d kfc_db -t emp -Fd -f emp				#directory format, parallelism 

exmaples.,

pg_dump -U kfc_user -d kfc_db -t emp -Fc -f emp1.bkp -Z 9
pg_dump -U kfc_user -d kfc_db -t emp -Fc -f emp1.bkp -Z lz4:9
pg_dump -U kfc_user -d kfc_db -t emp -Fc -f emp1.bkp -Z gzip:9

restore your backup using pg_restore
------------------------------------
/usr/pgsql-18/bin/pg_restore -U kfc_user -d kfc_db emp.bk


